{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: archive operator restart (deployment-only, identity-bound restart of an eligible stopped-limit archive row) at exact head 5f4c98bd6644068ce0bd0a8883d738eaa712c1ae, tree b6ff4b88a32d7125c290672ff07c15e4467123d2 (review request 7d6d37f3, promise aa421514, implementation ea0152b3 / builder promise 756cfd9b, decision fc040366). It may land. Deployment is planner-owned and carries the notes at the end.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-24-archive-operator-restart.md (artifact bfb6cb7b), first and in full, then the twelve supporting artifacts at this head: archive-restart.ts (new), archive-row.ts, archive-driver.ts, archive-operator.ts, object.ts, apps/room/archive.ts, worker.grow.ts, test/worker.ts, the three archive test files and scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs. The worktree is clean at the head. The merge-base with Main is Main itself, 0fae5159; the head is eight commits above it, including a merge of the landed bearer-expiry work. The gate head bc668d68 (tree 4e234b11) differs from the final head only in the implementation note, so gate 83102 carries without a repeat (docs/testing.md:597).\n\nConditions of ea0152b3 and fc040366, each checked in source:\n1. Exact scope and repository: readArchiveRestart requires a canonical JSON payload of at most 8 KiB with the closed field set v, command, at, repository, format, confirmed, rowDigest, generation, expires; command must equal the digest of the canonical payload without command; the driver requires same(command.at, current.at); ArchiveRows.restart refuses when at, repository, format or confirmed differ from the stored row. A recreated scope has a different at and a different receipt generation, so a stale directive is refused.\n2. Confirmed-v2 receipt and no pending Mark: restart refuses unless the row is stopped with reason \"limit\", pending is null, attempts is 0, next is null and confirmed has layout 2.\n3. CAS on the canonical row: one SELECT fences the exact row bytes (typeof text, exact octet_length, byte-equal cast) and the exact receipt bytes, or NOT EXISTS when no receipt was ever written; any mismatch returns archive-row-conflict and the transaction writes nothing. The directive also carries rowDigest, which must equal the digest of the stored row bytes.\n4. Keep receipt and frontier, restore the retry wake in the same write: inside one transaction the row is saved with stopped null and everything else unchanged, the wake row becomes {pending true, stopped false, next}, and the restart receipt becomes {v 1, generation prior+1, command}. No frontier key is touched; the row witness checks frontier bytes before and after, and the driver witness checks frontier keys and head.\n5. Operator only: the setting is ARCHIVE_RESTART_DIRECTIVE, a nonsecret deployment setting read by worker.grow.ts and forwarded through Wiring.archiveRestart; no route, RPC, service binding or room act can reach it. Only the Grow Worker reads it.\n6. Witness on the real operator path: the driver witness runs a real Native lane, a labelled limit stop, the directive through the fixture map in test/worker.ts, ordinary ingress, the diagnostic line, the restart, the alarm at the exact wake and a confirmed pass through head. The row witness covers parser refusals, every identity mismatch, every ineligible row shape, receipt-write rollback, the raced row and the read-only replay.\n7. Gate once before review: gate 83102 at bc668d68.\n\nCode conclusions. The transition lives in one place: ScopeObject.#recoverArchiveAlarm calls this.#archive.restart(directive) after the activation diagnostic has completed, only while no alarm runs and no recovery is in flight, and only when the scope status is active; the call is synchronous and precedes the wake lookup, so a restart that applies is followed in the same ingress by the alarm being set for next. ArchiveDriver.restart refuses when the driver is running, disabled, or has no policies, when the parser refuses, when at differs, and on any throw. ArchiveRows.restart orders its checks so that a replay (prior.command equals command.command and prior.generation equals command.generation plus one) returns \"already-applied\" before the row snapshot is loaded, and a generation mismatch returns \"refused\"; after an applied restart the setting costs one small meta read per ingress until the planner removes it. next is #later(0), one second, so a restart only clears the stop and schedules the normal retry; the deferral and backoff cadence governs from there. The diagnostic line gains rowDigest (only for stopped-limit rows with no pending Mark; null for private reasons) and restartGeneration, which together with at, repository, format and confirmed are everything the planner needs to compose a directive. The seal file adds archive-restart.ts and re-seals the six touched production files; every seal equals the actual-values file at the head.\n\nEvidence verified. Gate 83102 raw (expectedHead bc668d68, tree 4e234b11, unchanged checkpoint, gatePassed, before and after equal, eight stages exit 0, 497 test files passed and 1 skipped, 3,548 tests passed and 3 skipped, Node 39/0, Counting 55/0, no unhandled errors); gate audit manifest e8239b47, closed-validation audit manifest 0a418e80 and consumption-control audit manifest 64216808 verified by sha256 over every listed file; terminal cases for the driver, row, operator and item-query-owned suites all passed, including both new witnesses. Consumption control 88369 replaced the restart call in object.ts with void and left the driver witness red at archive-driver.test.ts:552 (stopped stays reason limit) with 18 passes, child exit 1 and owner exit 0; the mutated file's original digest equals the head's object.ts; the restoration leaves differ only in cache and identity cells. Head digests of the seven touched production files match the control's snapshot where the control read them.\n\nDocument checks at 5f4c98bd:\n- git diff --check from Main 0fae5159 is clean;\n- check-commit-messages from 0fae5159 reports 8 checked, 0 flagged; the longest subject is 54 characters;\n- section citations on an export report 1,877 resolved, 0 broken and 5 known unresolved; the citation script is identical to Main's;\n- merging the head into Main 0fae5159 gives exactly its tree, b6ff4b88.\n- Status sentences in the note are its dated report form (review and deployment pending), accepted as for the earlier heads today; nothing in it is false on landing.\n\nArchitecture: one deployment-only transition, consumed on existing ingress after the diagnostic, with a generation-chained receipt in the existing meta table; no new entry point, no journal write, no host call. The directive is bound to the row it names and expires, so it cannot survive to a later stop. This is the smallest shape that meets fc040366.\n\nSecurity: the setting is nonsecret and that is sound, because possession of the directive grants nothing beyond what the deployment principal already holds, it names one scope and one exact row state, and it is inert on every other object. Replay is read-only; a later stop with the same command is refused through the generation and digest checks. Malformed, oversized, extra-field or expired payloads fail closed to \"refused\" without a write. No secret or token is introduced.\n\nSimplification: nonblocking. The expiry check is made twice (parser and row); the generation ceiling guard is theoretical. Both are cheap and harmless.\n\nResidual notes for the planner's deploy, not defects of this head: read the deployed diagnostic to take at, repository, format, confirmed, rowDigest and restartGeneration; choose a short absolute expiry; compute command as the digest of the canonical payload without command; set ARCHIVE_RESTART_DIRECTIVE on dap-grow only, and remove it once the diagnostic shows restartGeneration advanced. Deploy the landed deferral, diagnostic and backoff heads first, since the restart relies on their cadence and on the diagnostic fields. Hosted MCP stays closed unless MCP_ENABLED is set (10f45efc).\n\nFindings: none blocking. Nothing is deployed or claimed deployed by this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bfb6cb7b9fa506c334efc9a697909c89cafbfa00","binding":"assigned","head":"5f4c98bd6644068ce0bd0a8883d738eaa712c1ae","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:aa421514caaacefad9eb1ae168c7c32d2243ae0a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:756cfd9bbfff10491c90e6ca43ff7ae1d8cb653c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f7b83c19bce36493f1b7fbb0981eabc2dd55be0f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}